d and integrated metrology systems, silicon wafer all-surface inspection, macro defect inspection, automated defect classification and pattern analysis, yield analysis, opaque film metrology, 4D business, advanced packaging lithography, process control software, and yield management software products. It also provides process and yield management solutions, and device packaging and test facilities through standalone systems for optical metrology, macro-defect inspection, packaging lithography, and transparent and opaque thin film measurements. In addition, the company offers process control software portfolio that includes solutions for standalone tools, groups of tools, and factory-wide suites. Further, it engages in systems and software, spare parts, and other services, as well as offers software licensing services; and provides advanced product lines, such as FAaST, CnCV, and MBIR. The company's products are used in semiconductor and advanced packaging device manufacturers; silicon wafers; semiconductor integrated circuit fabricators; light emitting diodes; vertical-cavity surface-emitting lasers; micro-electromechanical systems; CMOS image sensors; silicon and compound semiconductor power devices; analog devices; RF filters; data storage; and various industrial and scientific applications. Onto Innovation Inc. was founded in 1940 and is headquartered in Wilmington, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael P. Plisinski | CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $529K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 12%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $115K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $15K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Onto Innovation Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $8.5B market cap on $987M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +21% over the past three years and +19% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 52% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $214M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 22 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.22\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.3%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 73% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7333437409819096},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How to Approach Onto Innovation Stock Ahead of Q3 Earnings?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025618/how-to-approach-onto-innovation-stock-ahead-of-q3-earnings?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cmost_popular_stocks-3025618","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793974560.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Stay Ahead of the Game With Onto Innovation (ONTO) Q3 Earnings: Wall Street's Insights on Key Metrics","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3022795/stay-ahead-of-the-game-with-onto-innovation-onto-q3-earnings-wall-street-s-insights-on-key-metrics?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm_preview-3022795","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793798109.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Onto Innovation (ONTO) Nears Earnings With Analyst Optimism, Is The Valuation Still Too Rich?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/semiconductors/nyse-onto/onto-innovation/news/onto-innovation-onto-nears-earnings-with-analyst-optimism-is","date":"2026-11-04